WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:05.680
To be CS:GO’d is to be rekt, to be wronged,
to be utterly destroyed,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.420
through no fault of your own, by the one they call Valve.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.520
Now the traditional definition of getting CS:GO’d
involves putting your crosshair over somebody’s

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.080
head, pulling the trigger, and having the
bullets go through them like nothing happened.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.000
But for the purposes of this video, we’ve
expanded the definition to include those pesky

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.900
bugs, those glitches, and the general what-the-f--kery
that has happened in pro play.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.780
So let’s get it started with the traditional
definition of getting CS:GO’d.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:02:03.780
(Casting)

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:09.340
Now, while getting CS:GO’d can really make
your blood boil, arguably worse are the random

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:15.280
seemingly unpredictable bugs that can cost you
your life, the round, and even the game.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:05:10.720
(Casting)

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.160
Now, to round this one out guys, we wanted to look at some of the more lighthearted glitches in the game of CS:GO.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.060
This kind of stuff you can’t even be mad at, you just have to sit back and laugh.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:06:40.520
(Casting)

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:43.200
"It's just a flesh wound."

00:06:43.200 --> 00:08:17.720
(Casting)

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.520
Well guys, that’s all we’ve got for you this week on Best of.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:34.760
Now, this particular installment is really near and dear to my heart, because I’m always getting CS:GO’d in my games.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:38.120
Nobody in the office even believes me. But you guys do, right???

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.640
Let me know in the comments and I will see you next week.

